---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { DIGUP_UI, SITE } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Layout
  title={'Install DigUp on Windows (0.7 Beta) — Setup Guide'}
  description={'How to install DigUp 0.7 beta on 64-bit Windows 10/11: download DigUp_0.7.0-beta.1_x64-setup.exe, SmartScreen "Run anyway," model download, and Ctrl+Shift+Space.'}
  canonicalPath="/install-windows/"
  lang="en"
  ogImage={DIGUP_UI.pdf.src}
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="meta-line"><span class="badge">Windows · beta</span> · Install guide</p>
      <h1>Install DigUp on Windows</h1>
      <p class="lead">DigUp <strong>{SITE.downloads.windowsVersion}</strong> brings the same EmbeddingGemma 2 search to 64-bit Windows 10/11. This is a beta — expect rough edges. Download the installer asset directly.</p>
    </header>

    <article class="wide">
      <div class="callout" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
        <strong>Beta label.</strong> Windows builds have had far less field time than Mac 0.6.1. Use the Windows installer download below.
      </div>

      <div class="cta-bar">
        <a class="cta" href={SITE.downloads.windows} rel="noopener noreferrer" download>Download DigUp for Windows</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/install-mac/">Mac (stable)</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/install-linux/">Linux (beta)</a>
      </div>

      <p>First run downloads EmbeddingGemma 2 (~865 MB via llama.cpp). Model details: <a href="/embeddinggemma-2/">EmbeddingGemma 2 in DigUp</a> · <a href="/guides/embeddinggemma-2-local-multimodal-search/">multimodal guide</a>.</p>

      <h2>Requirements</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Item</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>OS</strong></td><td>64-bit Windows 10 or 11</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Installer</strong></td><td>Per-user; no admin rights required</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Signing</strong></td><td>Installer not signed yet → SmartScreen “More info” → <strong>Run anyway</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Asset</strong></td><td><code>DigUp_0.7.0-beta.1_x64-setup.exe</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Model</strong></td><td>~865 MB download on first launch</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Install checklist</h2>
      <ol class="checklist">
        <li>Download <a href={SITE.downloads.windows} rel="noopener noreferrer" download><code>DigUp_0.7.0-beta.1_x64-setup.exe</code></a>.</li>
        <li>Run the installer. If Windows SmartScreen appears: <strong>More info</strong> → <strong>Run anyway</strong>.</li>
        <li>Launch DigUp. Let the model download while you pick folders to search.</li>
        <li>Note the first-pass time estimate for your machine.</li>
        <li>Open search from any app with <strong>Ctrl+Shift+Space</strong>.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>GPU vs CPU</h2>
      <p>DigUp runs a quick check and uses the GPU when it is faster and gives the same results; otherwise it uses the CPU. On CPU alone, pictures take a few seconds each — large photo libraries take longer the first time. After that, only new files are read.</p>
      <p>To confirm which device was chosen, open the last line of <code>speed.log</code>:</p>
      <pre><code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\com.arahim3.digup\logs\speed.log</code></pre>
      <p class="muted">Look for <code>"device": "gpu"</code> or <code>"device": "cpu"</code>. Path may vary by build — check DigUp Settings / docs if missing.</p>

      <h2>Beta limits (0.7.0-beta.1)</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>No screenshot OCR text yet</strong> — screenshots are found by what they show, not by typing the on-screen code into search.</li>
        <li><strong>Skipped on this beta:</strong> old Word <code>.doc</code>, RAW photos, SVG.</li>
        <li>Self-updating installer / AppImage path exists going forward; always confirm behavior in current release notes.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sourced facts (2026-10-15)</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Fact</th><th>Value</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Tag</td><td>v0.7.0-beta.1 (prerelease)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Published</td><td>2026-10-14 (UTC)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Mac stays at</td><td>0.6.1 (not in the 0.7 Windows/Linux release bundle)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Upstream stars</td><td>~3,716</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="cta-bar">
        <a class="cta" href={SITE.downloads.windows} rel="noopener noreferrer" download>Download DigUp for Windows</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/changelog-notes/">Changelog notes</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/faq/">FAQ</a>
      </div>

      
      <h2>Sourced snapshot (2026-10-15)</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Fact</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Tag</td><td>v0.7.0-beta.1</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Windows setup downloads</td><td>~135 (scan)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Mac DMG 0.6.1 downloads</td><td>~4,689</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Stars</td><td>~3,768</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Gaps on this beta</td><td>No screenshot OCR text; skip .doc / RAW / SVG</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Thick first-week guide: <a href="/guides/win-linux-beta/">Win/Linux beta</a>. Not affiliated with ARahim3.</p>

      <h2>GPU check via <code>speed.log</code></h2>
      <p>After first launch, open the last line of DigUp’s <code>speed.log</code> (folder under local app data — see release notes if path differs) and confirm <code>"device": "gpu"</code> or <code>"cpu"</code>. Include that line when filing upstream issues.</p>

      <section class="related">
        <h2>Related</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          <a class="card" href="/install-linux/"><h3>Linux install</h3><p>Same beta train</p></a>
          <a class="card" href="/what-is-digup/"><h3>What is DigUp?</h3><p>Modalities &amp; architecture</p></a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
